From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +01:00
Subject: [PATCH] feat: bind admitted pods to reserved nodeclaims via anti-theft taints and tolerations

When Kueue admits multi-slice elastic workloads on dynamic capacity, long-lived job templates retain the first slice's Karpenter anti-theft attempt node selector and taints, causing subsequent slices to inherit stale node placement. Simultaneously, newly created pods held by the elastic scheduling gate do not receive admission check tolerations from ElasticJobUngater before ungating, preventing them from scheduling onto nodes guarded by anti-theft taints.

Strip per-attempt Karpenter node selectors and anti-theft tolerations from elastic job pod templates via deferKarpenterPlacementToPods so subsequent slices do not inherit stale placement. In ElasticJobUngater, inject admission check tolerations onto gated elastic pods before releasing their scheduling gates when KarpenterAdmissionCheck is enabled.
---
